    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I've successfully fixed the floating-point rounding issue in three places:\n\n1. **src/money.js (parseEuros)**: Changed `Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100)`\n2. **src/money.js (cellCents)**: Changed `Number(s) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s) * 100)`\n3. **src/locale.js (decimalCommaToCents)**: Changed `parseFloat(...) * 100` to `Math.round(parseFloat(...) * 100)`\n\nThe issue was that JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic causes `39.95 * 100` to equal `3995.0000000000005` instead of `3995`. Using `Math.round()` fixes this by rounding to the nearest whole number, which is the standard approach for handling monetary values.\n\nI've tested it and verified:\n- \u2705 Adding Gym at 39.95 now works\n- \u2705 Netflix (12.99) still works\n- \u2705 Spotify (10.99) still works\n\nThe changes are ready to commit. Would you like me to create a git commit with these changes?",
